0,Panoan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panoan_languages,"Panoan (also Pánoan, Panoano, Panoana, Páno) is a family of languages spoken in western Brazil, eastern Peru, and northern Bolivia. It is a branch of a larger Pano–Tacanan family.",Atsahuaca,Panoan
1,Atsawaka language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atsawaka_language,"Atswawaka, also called Atsahuaca, or Atsawaka-Yamiaka, is an extinct Panoan language of Peru. Atsahuaca is the name that the tribe calls themselves, meaning ""children of the manioc "" in their own language.",Atsahuaca,Panoan
2,Atsahuaca Language and the Atsahuaca Indian Tribe (Atsahuacas),https://www.native-languages.org/atsahuaca.htm,"Language: Atsahuaca was a Panoan language of South America, once spoken in southeastern Peru. A neighboring language, Yamiaca, may have been an Atsahuaca dialect.",Atsahuaca,Panoan
